From: OpenHarmony PC porting (libomptarget-rtl-amdgpu 18.1.8)
Subject: [PATCH] openmp/amdgpu: accept HarmonyOS as a linux-like plugin host

The AMDGPU nextgen plugin gates its build on CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME matching
"Linux".  OpenHarmony/HarmonyOS reports CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=HarmonyOS (kernel
is linux-based, toolchain targets aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos), so the gate
silently returned() and the plugin was never built on this platform.

Accept the HarmonyOS system name alongside Linux.  No behavior change on
other platforms.

--- a/openmp/libomptarget/plugins-nextgen/amdgpu/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/openmp/libomptarget/plugins-nextgen/amdgpu/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 find_package(hsa-runtime64 QUIET 1.2.0 HINTS ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX} PATHS /opt/rocm)
 
-if(NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "(x86_64)|(ppc64le)|(aarch64)$" AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux"))
-  libomptarget_say("Not building AMDGPU NextGen plugin: only support AMDGPU in Linux x86_64, ppc64le, or aarch64 hosts")
+if(NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "(x86_64)|(ppc64le)|(aarch64)$" AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "(Linux|HarmonyOS)"))
+  libomptarget_say("Not building AMDGPU NextGen plugin: only support AMDGPU in Linux/HarmonyOS x86_64, ppc64le, or aarch64 hosts")
   return()
 endif()
 
